{"id":"9af64ac4f14ac427","group":"73","path":"73/73-thm-binary-reduction-recognizability.md","title":"Many-One Reduction Preserves Recognizability Downward","display":"thm-many-one-reduction-preserves-recognizability — Many-One Reduction Preserves Recognizability Downward","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Introduction to Automata Theory, Languages, and Computation (Hopcroft, Motwani, Ullman; 3rd ed., 2007)","book_abbrev":"73","label":"73-thm-binary-reduction-recognizability","aliases":["73-thm-binary-reduction-recognizability","73-thm-many-one-reduction-preserves-recognizability"],"display":"thm-many-one-reduction-preserves-recognizability — Many-One Reduction Preserves Recognizability Downward","depends_on":["[[73-df-binary-many-one-reduction]]","[[73-df-dtm-recognizable-languages]]"],"source_id":"HMU2007","source_ref":"§9.3, print pp. 390–401; PDF pp. 412–423; local typed effective reduction/coding","source_status":"third-edition-topic-mapped; inherited-local-review; not-a-line-by-line-source-proof-certificate","reviewed_on":"2026-10-24","legacy_source_id":"HU1979","legacy_source_ref":"§8.4–8.7, pp. 185–207; local total computable reduction abstraction","legacy_source_status":"local-formalization; source-section-located; proof scope recorded in review","revision_round":"pdf-third-edition-20261024","edition_role":"third-edition-core","third_edition_chapter":9},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Introduction to Automata Theory, Languages, and Computation (Hopcroft, Motwani, Ullman; 3rd ed., 2007)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"73"},{"key":"label","html":"73-thm-binary-reduction-recognizability"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>73-thm-binary-reduction-recognizability</span><span>73-thm-many-one-reduction-preserves-recognizability</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-many-one-reduction-preserves-recognizability — Many-One Reduction Preserves Recognizability Downward"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"64d902370bb28edb\" href=\"?note=64d902370bb28edb\" title=\"73-df-binary-many-one-reduction\">73-df-binary-many-one-reduction</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"11b19b6d211be8ab\" href=\"?note=11b19b6d211be8ab\" title=\"73-df-dtm-recognizable-languages\">73-df-dtm-recognizable-languages</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_id","html":"HMU2007"},{"key":"source_ref","html":"§9.3, print pp. 390–401; PDF pp. 412–423; local typed effective reduction/coding"},{"key":"source_status","html":"third-edition-topic-mapped; inherited-local-review; not-a-line-by-line-source-proof-certificate"},{"key":"reviewed_on","html":"2026-10-24"},{"key":"legacy_source_id","html":"HU1979"},{"key":"legacy_source_ref","html":"§8.4–8.7, pp. 185–207; local total computable reduction abstraction"},{"key":"legacy_source_status","html":"local-formalization; source-section-located; proof scope recorded in review"},{"key":"revision_round","html":"pdf-third-edition-20261024"},{"key":"edition_role","html":"third-edition-core"},{"key":"third_edition_chapter","html":"9"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\leq_m\">\\(\\leq_m\\)</span> (computable many-one reducibility, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"64d902370bb28edb\" href=\"?note=64d902370bb28edb\" title=\"73-df-binary-many-one-reduction\">73-df-binary-many-one-reduction</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{RE}_{\\mathbf 2}\">\\(\\mathsf{RE}_{\\mathbf 2}\\)</span> (recognizable binary languages, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"11b19b6d211be8ab\" href=\"?note=11b19b6d211be8ab\" title=\"73-df-dtm-recognizable-languages\">73-df-dtm-recognizable-languages</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}many\\text{-}one\\text{-}reduction\\text{-}preserves\\text{-}recognizability}\\vdash\n\\forall A,B\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*\\;\n\\bigl(A\\leq_m B\\land B\\in\\mathsf{RE}_{\\mathbf 2}\n\\longrightarrow A\\in\\mathsf{RE}_{\\mathbf 2}\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}many\\text{-}one\\text{-}reduction\\text{-}preserves\\text{-}recognizability}\\vdash\n\\forall A,B\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*\\;\n\\bigl(A\\leq_m B\\land B\\in\\mathsf{RE}_{\\mathbf 2}\n\\longrightarrow A\\in\\mathsf{RE}_{\\mathbf 2}\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>On input <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x\">\\(x\\)</span>, first compute the total reduction value <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f(x)\">\\(f(x)\\)</span> and then run a recognizer for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B\">\\(B\\)</span>. It accepts exactly when <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x\\in A\">\\(x\\in A\\)</span>; divergence on negative instances is permitted.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"73-df-binary-many-one-reduction","status":"resolved","id":"64d902370bb28edb","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-binary-many-one-reduction]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-dtm-recognizable-languages","status":"resolved","id":"11b19b6d211be8ab","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-dtm-recognizable-languages]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-binary-many-one-reduction","status":"resolved","id":"64d902370bb28edb","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\leq_m$ (computable many-one reducibility, see [[73-df-binary-many-one-reduction]])","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-dtm-recognizable-languages","status":"resolved","id":"11b19b6d211be8ab","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathsf{RE}_{\\mathbf 2}$ (recognizable binary languages, see [[73-df-dtm-recognizable-languages]])","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"\\leq_m","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathsf{RE}_{\\mathbf 2}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}many\\text{-}one\\text{-}reduction\\text{-}preserves\\text{-}recognizability}\\vdash\n\\forall A,B\\subseteq\\mathbf 2^*\\;\n\\bigl(A\\leq_m B\\land B\\in\\mathsf{RE}_{\\mathbf 2}\n\\longrightarrow A\\in\\mathsf{RE}_{\\mathbf 2}\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"x","display":false},{"tex":"f(x)","display":false},{"tex":"B","display":false},{"tex":"x\\in A","display":false}],"bytes":1842,"backlinks":[{"id":"6af52783a9bce985","anchor":"ref-217","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[73-thm-binary-reduction-recognizability|Many-One Reduction Preserves Recognizability Downward]]"},{"id":"de6518bc0894c6c3","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""}],"outgoing":["64d902370bb28edb","11b19b6d211be8ab"]}